TITLE:: RAStereoMonitor
summary:: FOA cardioid stereo decode of an RAOutputChain
categories:: Libraries>reAmbi
related:: Guides/reAmbi, Classes/RAOutputChain

DESCRIPTION::
A stereo monitor for the PA: the first-order part of the stage feeding the chain's decoder is high-passed, proximity-compensated and decoded with link::Classes/FoaDecoderMatrix#*newStereo:: to two channels on strong::outBus::. Registered on a chain with link::Classes/RAOutputChain#-addMonitor::, built and cleared with it; its configuration survives a clear. The chain re-taps the monitor when stages are inserted, removed or moved.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: outBus
argument:: ampDb
Gain in dB (a control on the proxy, adjustable live).
argument:: hpFreq
argument:: angleDeg
Stereo decoder angle in degrees.
argument:: pattern
Microphone pattern of the decoder (0.5 = cardioid).
argument:: fadeTime

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: build
argument:: chain
METHOD:: clear
METHOD:: isBuilt
